{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"087d679e636e08063ee24ae523a193d831c5eb83530e7e4d4788bba6748c3e31","digest":{"component_or_area":"Reconciler JQL builders (fetcher.py)","key_entities":["fetcher.py","jql_active","jql_done_recent","statusCategory","status != Done","status = Done","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_paging_split.py","Gerrit change 1815"],"problem_keywords":["reconciler","active set scoping","status category","jql query","workflow","done equivalent","closed resolved cancelled"],"propositions":["The reconciler hardcodes status != 'Done' in jql_active and status = 'Done' in jql_done_recent, which fails to recognize custom Done-equivalent statuses (Closed, Resolved, Cancelled) used in non-standard Jira workflows.","Issues in Done-category statuses outside the literal 'Done' status are incorrectly included in the active working set, causing the reconciler to treat resolved issues as active and push mutations at them.","Switching jql_active to statusCategory != Done and jql_done_recent to statusCategory = Done makes the active-set scoping workflow-agnostic and correctly covers all Done-equivalent statuses across projects.","The statusCategory predicate is supported in both Jira Cloud and Data Center and correctly maps all custom statuses to their respective categories."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787640353588250001,"uuid":"112dc711-da83-4e75-8938-df8fcfd01576"}